{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Memories of Things Past"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The House on Cranberry Lane"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le11ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Perfect for Unfulfilled Action "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " The Past Perfect tense is in reality, the past of the past. You use it to say that an action was completed before another action took place. Both the actions are related to each other in some way. The action already completed is expressed by the Past Perfect tense. The action which takes place later is expressed by the Simple Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Past Perfect to talk about unfulfilled actions in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I <span class=\"strong\">had worked</span> harder, I would have been promoted.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Past Perfect construction is part of the third conditional - which refers to an unreal situation in the past. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here's another example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">John <span class=\"strong\">had hoped</span> to get a promotion, but he didn't work hard enough.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "For them it was the house that had held all their memories until they left."}, {"type": "example", "content": "After they had gone fishing in the local river, pretending they were fly-fishing experts, they had often come back empty-handed but happy."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When they had found a new secret hiding places in the area where no one could find them, they had disappeared for hours."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Edward and Robert had tried to visit often, but as time went on, their lives became more hectic and time seemed to evaporate."}, {"type": "example", "content": "After their mother had passed away, they tried to convince their father to move closer to one of them, but he refused."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Perfect Infinitives for Unreal Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use Perfect Infinitives in the same way as you use other Perfect tenses (to talk about the past). You can use them to to talk about unreal situations in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If you <span class=\"strong\">were to have asked</span>, I would have helped. </span>(You didn't ask and I didn't help.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">was meant to have asked</span> my permission before using my computer. </span>(He did not ask my permission.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If she <span class=\"strong\">were to have become</span> a nurse, she could work here with us. </span>(She has not become a nurse.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">would like to have sent</span> her flowers.</span> (He didn't send flowers but he wanted to.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You need to be aware of the context when using modals in this way since some of them can also be used to talk about probability and certainty."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">could have/should have arrived</span> by now. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There was never a dull moment in the Harmer household if the truth were to have been told."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they were to have fought, they always made up quickly."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If anyone were to have described them, they would have said they were inseparable"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they were to have accidentally thrown a football through a neighbor's windows, or happened to have poured bleach onto Mrs. Jones' prized rose bushes, or were found to have slathered shaving cream all over Uncle Bart's car, they would have been in trouble."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to make up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bforgive someone after an \u200bargument or \u200bdisagreement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If they were to have fought, they always made up quickly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about a childhood home."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "never a dull moment"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something is always changing or happening"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was never a dull moment in the Harmer household."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inseparable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "always together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They would have said they were inseparable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "barefoot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without shoes or socks"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The energetic brothers spent their summers running around together barefoot."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fly-fishing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the sport of fishing using a rod and an artificial fly as bait"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They had gone fishing in the local river, pretending they were fly-fishing experts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prized"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "highly valued"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They happened to have poured bleach onto Mrs. Jones' prized rose bushes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to slather"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spread"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They were found to have slathered shaving cream all over Uncle Bart's car."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob05aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get away with murder"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "succeed in doing whatever one chooses without being punished or suffering any disadvantage "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Somehow they had always managed to get away with murder."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le11ob05aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find a picture in the internet or in a magazine of a house with a yard that looks interesting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the house and the area around it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you lived in that house and area as a child and say what you and a friend or sibling did with your free time there."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain what you liked about the area and house."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write about 200 words in total."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use sentences that express an unfulfilled action or wish in the past."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I choose a picture of a house and describe it and the area around it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write an imaginary account of what a friend or sibling and I did in the house and area."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Past Simple and the Past perfect."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about relationships and character traits."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express an unfulfilled action or wish in the past."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about unreal past situations."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What type of place did you grow up in?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are some of your fondest memories of your childhood there?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}