, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}], "id": 10}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn11le11ob05re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Talk about a childhood home."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn11le11ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "Edward and Robert Harmer grew up in the house on Cranberry Lane. Their great-grandfather had built the house in 1850. This was the house their grandfather and their father had been born in as well. For them it was the house that had held all their memories until they left.<br/>\nThere was never a dull moment in the Harmer household, if the truth were to have been told. The boys had always been close as children. If they were to have fought, they always made up quickly. If anyone were to have described them, they would have said they were inseparable. The energetic brothers spent their summers running around together barefoot.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn11le11ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "40000", "text": "After they had gone fishing in the local river, pretending they were fly-fishing experts, they had often come back empty-handed but happy. When they had found a new secret hiding place in the area where no one could find them, they had disappeared for hours. They often really needed a hiding places too, because they were constantly in trouble, much to the dismay of their parents. <br/>\nIf they were to have accidentally thrown a football through a neighbor's window, or happened to have poured bleach onto Mrs. Jones' prized rose bushes, or were to have slathered shaving cream all over Uncle Bart's car, they would have been in trouble. Somehow they had always managed to get away with murder.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn11le11ob05re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "82500", "text": "Everything had changed when they got older. Both were sure they would have more time to spend together, but they did not. They were busy living their own lives, and the house on Cranberry Lane grew quiet. Edward and Robert had tried to visit often, but as time went on, their lives became more hectic and time seemed to evaporate.<br/>\nAfter their mother had passed away, they tried to convince their father to move closer to one of them, but he refused. In only a few short months, Thomas Harmer died in his sleep in the great big bed that he was born in. That was when trouble began.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn11le11ob05re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le11ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le11ob05re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": []}]}]}